course: dictionary
lesson: 11779
title: Bedraggled
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Bedraggled» describes something wet, dirty and messy, like a cat that has been out in the rain and mud. It can also describe a person or thing that looks worn out and untidy after a hard time.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «The bedraggled kitten shivered on the doorstep after the storm.» Wet and shivering are clues, so bedraggled must mean wet and messy. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «The wet, messy kitten shivered on the doorstep» still makes sense.
explain: The second meaning comes from how someone looks and feels. «The bedraggled team trudged off the pitch, muddy and sorry for themselves.» Muddy shows the mess, and sorry for themselves shows how they feel. Stories use bedraggled to show that a character has had a hard time.
fact: Bedraggled means wet, dirty and messy.
fact: It can describe a thing or a person who looks untidy, worn out and sorry for themselves.
fact: «A bedraggled teddy» is a teddy left out in the rain, soggy and muddy.
fact: In Alice's Adventures in Wonderland, the birds and animals come out of the Pool of Tears looking bedraggled, with wet fur and draggled feathers.
exercise: «The bedraggled cat sat under the hedge after the storm.» What does bedraggled mean here? | Bright and shiny | *Wet, dirty and messy | Very loud and noisy | Brand new
exercise: Ben says his teddy looks bedraggled after it was left out all night. What does he mean? | *Wet, dirty and messy from being left out | Happy and proud | Very tall and thin | Freshly washed and dry
exercise: «After the long match, the bedraggled players looked tired and sorry for themselves.» Find and copy one word that is a clue to the second meaning. | *tired | match | players | long
test: «The bedraggled birds shook their wet feathers and waited to dry.» Which clue shows the birds are bedraggled? | *Wet feathers | Singing loudly | Bright colours | Flying high
test: Which sentence uses bedraggled correctly? | The bedraggled sun shone brightly over the bay. | The bedraggled trophy gleamed on the shelf. | The bedraggled sweets were bright and new in their wrappers. | *The bedraggled coat hung on the peg, soaked and muddy from the field.
exam: Which word means the same as bedraggled? | Bright | *Soggy and untidy | Quiet | Smart
